{"nodes": [{"id": "backend_md", "label": "Especifica\u00e7\u00e3o t\u00e9cnica do backend (normativa)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This document specifies the technical backend requirements."}, {"id": "docs_backend_md", "label": "Especifica\u00e7\u00e3o T\u00e9cnica do Backend", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This document outlines the technical specification for the backend, detailing how the backend fulfills each promise made in the UX/UI specification."}, {"id": "adr_01", "label": "O host \u00e9 a \u00fanica autoridade de escrita", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-01", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR specifies that the host is the sole authority for writing, ensuring total grace, applicability of permissions/hierarchy/ban, and resolving issues related to clock synchronization, role management, and community management."}, {"id": "adr_02", "label": "Hypercore cru como log + SQLite como view materializada", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-02", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR chooses Hypercore for logging and SQLite for materialized views, reducing the surface to 5 stable packages in the ecosystem and avoiding issues with other packages like hyperdb, hyperdrive, and hyperbee."}, {"id": "adr_03", "label": "Driver SQLite = `better-sqlite3@13`", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-03", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR selects `better-sqlite3@13` as the SQLite driver due to its synchronous API, which is exactly what the projector needs, and its extensive documentation and production history."}, {"id": "adr_04", "label": "N\u00facleo P2P em `utilityProcess` do Electron", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-04", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR places the P2P core in the `utilityProcess` of Electron to isolate RocksDB and the event loop from Chromium, preventing crashes of native addons from affecting the main window."}, {"id": "adr_05", "label": "M\u00eddia h\u00edbrida", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-05", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR uses WebRTC for voice/camera and WebCodecs for screen sharing over UDX streams in Hyperswarm, leveraging WebRTC's built-in features for echo cancellation, jitter buffer, FEC, and congestion control."}, {"id": "adr_06", "label": "Sem STUN de terceiros por padr\u00e3o", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-06", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR avoids exposing the IP of all participants to a third-party STUN server by using the public address of the node discovered by `hyperdht` and injecting it as an ICE candidate, with a default empty list of STUN servers."}, {"id": "adr_07", "label": "UDX \u00e9 o fallback universal de transporte", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-07", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR uses UDX as the universal fallback transport, providing a relay mechanism with three uses, covering cases where NAT traversal fails without a third-party TURN server and without paid infrastructure."}, {"id": "adr_08", "label": "Relay por volunt\u00e1rios", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-08", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR allows members to opt for running `blind-relay`, with the host registering volunteers in the log and `relayThrough` choosing by lower RTT. The host automatically joins the list if capable."}, {"id": "adr_09", "label": "Convite = segredo de 10 bytes (80 bits), 16 caracteres", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-09", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR specifies that an invite is a 10-byte secret (80 bits) encoded in 16 characters, ensuring a strong and unique identifier for community invitations."}, {"id": "adr_10", "label": "Fila de sa\u00edda (outbox) dur\u00e1vel em SQLite", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-10", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR uses a durable outbox in SQLite with exponential backoff and named terminal reasons, ensuring that messages are sent even if the host is offline."}, {"id": "adr_11", "label": "Idempot\u00eancia por `opId` = BLAKE2b-256 do envelope can\u00f4nico", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-11", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR ensures idempotency by using a `opId` derived from the canonical envelope, preventing duplicate messages on retransmission, reconnection, or manual retries."}, {"id": "adr_12", "label": "Busca full-text em SQLite FTS5", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-12", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR uses SQLite FTS5 for full-text search with a tokenizer and prefix index, providing efficient search capabilities for messages based on author, channel, date, and type."}, {"id": "adr_13", "label": "Presen\u00e7a, digitando e roster de voz s\u00e3o ef\u00eameros", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-13", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR ensures that presence, typing, and voice roster updates are ephemeral, stored only on `protomux` and never in the core, reducing the core size and avoiding unnecessary data replication."}, {"id": "adr_14", "label": "N\u00e3o-lidas e men\u00e7\u00f5es s\u00e3o c\u00e1lculo 100% local", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR ensures that unread and mentions are calculated 100% locally using a watermark of `seq` per channel, avoiding the need for cross-device synchronization."}, {"id": "adr_15", "label": "Toda comunidade participada replica em background", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR ensures that all communities participated in are replicated in the background, not just the active ones, providing a consistent and up-to-date view of all communities for the user."}, {"id": "adr_16", "label": "A \u00e1rvore de distribui\u00e7\u00e3o de tela \u00e9 calculada pelo host", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR centralizes the calculation of the screen distribution tree, replacing a distributed algorithm like SplitStream, ensuring that the host prioritizes the first levels as requested in CLAUDE.md."}, {"id": "adr_17", "label": "Sem notifica\u00e7\u00e3o com o app fechado no v1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR ensures that notifications are not sent when the app is closed, aligning with the UX specification's decision to exclude push notifications in the v1 release."}, {"id": "adr_18", "label": "Chave privada cifrada com `safeStorage` do Electron", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR ensures that the private key is encrypted using Electron's `safeStorage` (Keychain/DPAPI/libsecret), preventing it from being stored in plain text on the disk."}, {"id": "adr_19", "label": "Um \u00fanico processo n\u00facleo por instala\u00e7\u00e3o", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "1. Decis\u00f5es de arquitetura (ADR) -> ADR-19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This ADR ensures that there is only one process core per installation, using a directory lock to prevent multiple instances from running simultaneously."}, {"id": "docs_backend", "label": "Backend Rules", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This document outlines the backend rules and architecture."}, {"id": "docs_backend_category", "label": "Category", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "4.5 Category", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_backend_channel", "label": "Channel", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "4.6 Channel", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_backend_message", "label": "Message", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "4.7 Message", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_backend_thread", "label": "Thread", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "4.8 Thread", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_backend_reaction", "label": "Reaction", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "4.9 Reaction", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_backend_attachment", "label": "Attachment", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "4.10 Attachment", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_backend_invite", "label": "Invite", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/backend.md", "source_location": "4.11 Invite", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_backend_ban_timeout", "label": "Ban / Timeout", "file_type": "document", "source_fil